                            <comment id="15932981" author="amashenkov" created="Mon, 20 Mar 2017 16:32:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Seems, it happened with assertions disabled and when neither task nor its class not name was passed to GridTaskProcessor.startTask().&lt;br/&gt;
We should throw an exception with suited reason if task class name can&apos;t be resolved.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
